1
00:00:00,402 --> 00:00:03,505
♪ In the not too distant future ♪

2
00:00:03,572 --> 00:00:06,440
♪ Way down in Deep 13 ♪

3
00:00:06,507 --> 00:00:12,147
♪ Dr. Forrester and TV's Frank
Were hatching an evil scheme ♪

4
00:00:12,813 --> 00:00:15,817
♪ They hired a temp by the name of Mike ♪

5
00:00:15,883 --> 00:00:18,953
♪ Just a regular Joe they didn't like ♪

6
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:21,990
♪ Their experiment needed
A good test case ♪

7
00:00:22,057 --> 00:00:25,793
♪ So they conked him on the noggin
And they shot him into space ♪

8
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:28,262
[Mike] Get me down!

9
00:00:28,328 --> 00:00:33,502
♪ We'll send him cheesy movies
The worst we can find ♪

10
00:00:33,568 --> 00:00:34,568
♪ La-la-la ♪

11
00:00:34,635 --> 00:00:39,973
♪ He'll have to sit and watch them all
And we'll monitor his mind ♪

12
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,042
♪ La-la-la ♪

13
00:00:41,108 --> 00:00:43,878
♪ Now keep in mind
Mike can't control ♪

14
00:00:43,945 --> 00:00:45,947
♪ Where the movies begin or end ♪

15
00:00:46,013 --> 00:00:47,015
♪ La-la-la ♪

16
00:00:47,082 --> 00:00:52,920
♪ He'll try to keep his sanity
With the help of his robot friends ♪

17
00:00:55,223 --> 00:00:56,590
Robot roll call.

18
00:00:56,657 --> 00:00:58,092
-Cambot!
-Show yourself!

19
00:00:58,158 --> 00:00:59,427
-Gypsy!
-I'm not ready!

20
00:00:59,493 --> 00:01:01,262
-Tom Servo!
-Hello there!

21
00:01:01,328 --> 00:01:02,530
-Crow!
-That's one "O".

22
00:01:02,597 --> 00:01:05,833
♪ If you're wondering how
He eats and breathes ♪

23
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,868
♪ And other science facts ♪

24
00:01:07,935 --> 00:01:08,937
♪ La-la-la ♪

25
00:01:09,003 --> 00:01:11,973
♪ Just repeat to yourself
It's just a show ♪

26
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:14,908
♪ I should really just relax ♪

27
00:01:14,975 --> 00:01:20,315
♪ For Mystery Science Theater 3000 ♪

28
00:01:33,495 --> 00:01:36,597
-No, no. The plumb. Mike, the plum.
Mike, watch your plumb. Mike.

29
00:01:36,663 --> 00:01:38,232
-Yes, Servo, I know.

30
00:01:38,298 --> 00:01:40,968
-Uh, the pattern's
not matched up, Mike.

31
00:01:41,035 --> 00:01:43,672
Hey, you know, the pattern's not
matched up over there, either.

32
00:01:43,738 --> 00:01:45,807
-Thank you, Crow.
Thank you very much.

33
00:01:45,873 --> 00:01:46,942
Hi, everyone, I'm Mike.

34
00:01:47,008 --> 00:01:49,777
And, uh, Crow and Servo
here are helping me lots

35
00:01:49,843 --> 00:01:51,678
with my little
wallpapering project.

36
00:01:51,745 --> 00:01:53,748
-That's right. I thought this
would be a good way

37
00:01:53,815 --> 00:01:56,250
to give the place a
little perk me up. [laughs]

38
00:01:56,317 --> 00:01:58,285
We were gonna go with
the Christmas wallpaper.

39
00:01:58,352 --> 00:02:00,020
Then I put the kibosh on that.

40
00:02:00,087 --> 00:02:03,323
And it was very difficult to say
no to the birthday wallpaper,

41
00:02:03,390 --> 00:02:06,227
but I absolutely fell
in love with this.

42
00:02:06,293 --> 00:02:08,162
-Yes siree Bob,
we made the right choice.

43
00:02:08,228 --> 00:02:09,297
We gotta show Gypsy.

44
00:02:09,363 --> 00:02:11,632
Should we show Gypsy?
Hey, Gypsy!

45
00:02:11,698 --> 00:02:13,535
-Huh? Oh.

46
00:02:13,602 --> 00:02:14,602
Ooh.

47
00:02:14,668 --> 00:02:16,337
Oh, my God!

48
00:02:16,403 --> 00:02:19,607
Oh my, oh my, oh,
wrong, wrong, wrong!

49
00:02:19,673 --> 00:02:21,775
Oh, no! Oh, no! Oh, no!

50
00:02:21,843 --> 00:02:23,343
-[laughing] Oh, well.

51
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:26,280
Sometimes, a new look takes
a little getting used to.

52
00:02:26,347 --> 00:02:27,982
-We'll be right back.
-Yeah.

53
00:02:34,055 --> 00:02:35,657
-I think I still
see a place where

54
00:02:35,690 --> 00:02:37,325
the pattern's not
matched up, Mike.

55
00:02:37,392 --> 00:02:40,127
Although it is fun when we all
pitch in like this, isn't it?

56
00:02:40,195 --> 00:02:43,230
-Oh! I think the bads are calling.
-Really?

57
00:02:43,297 --> 00:02:44,932
-You know what I found out about you

58
00:02:44,998 --> 00:02:46,600
and your cute little friends, Nelson?

59
00:02:46,667 --> 00:02:48,670
You're part of the counterculture.
That's right!

60
00:02:48,737 --> 00:02:51,272
You're the enemy
of hard working guys like us.

61
00:02:51,605 --> 00:02:56,077
That's why today
is a great day.

62
00:02:56,143 --> 00:03:02,050
For today, we rally in support
of Proposition Deep 13.

63
00:03:02,350 --> 00:03:03,652
Thank you!

64
00:03:03,718 --> 00:03:05,052
Thank you!

65
00:03:05,118 --> 00:03:06,553
Thank you!

66
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:10,292
Simply put, Proposition Deep 13 means

67
00:03:10,358 --> 00:03:15,963
that we will send you today's experiment,
The Beast of Yucca Flats.

68
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:17,565
Thank you! Thank you!

69
00:03:17,632 --> 00:03:19,567
Thank you! Thank you.

70
00:03:19,633 --> 00:03:23,037
And it will crush
the Satellite of Love, Nelson,

71
00:03:23,103 --> 00:03:26,773
because we've signed a contract
with America.

72
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:28,743
Tell them what we're
sending them, Frank.

73
00:03:28,810 --> 00:03:31,445
-We're sending
you a wake up call

74
00:03:31,512 --> 00:03:34,615
named The Beast of Yucca Flats.

75
00:03:34,682 --> 00:03:36,717
-Take that, counterculture.

76
00:03:36,783 --> 00:03:40,187
-You're out of touch,
and we hate you.

77
00:03:40,255 --> 00:03:42,157
-Oh, you do, do you?

78
00:03:42,190 --> 00:03:44,225
Well, maybe we can't
match your pomp

79
00:03:44,292 --> 00:03:45,560
and your balloons
and your bunting.

80
00:03:45,627 --> 00:03:47,595
-Oh, hold on, I think I got a horn!

81
00:03:47,662 --> 00:03:51,432
-But what we do have here
is this man, the nation's most

82
00:03:51,498 --> 00:03:53,702
articulate spokesman
for the dream that is

83
00:03:53,768 --> 00:03:55,537
The Satellite of Love.

84
00:03:55,603 --> 00:03:58,072
This fearless man
who has led us,

85
00:03:58,138 --> 00:04:01,575
his quaking sheep, through,
lo, our darkest hours--

86
00:04:01,642 --> 00:04:02,843
-Thank you.
Thank you, Servo.

87
00:04:02,977 --> 00:04:04,778
-[making horn noises]

88
00:04:04,845 --> 00:04:07,882
-Need I describe how he stood
with us before the goons

89
00:04:07,948 --> 00:04:09,717
and truncheons of
Peabody Mining?

90
00:04:09,783 --> 00:04:11,785
A loyal friend to the unions!

91
00:04:11,852 --> 00:04:13,453
A--
-Get out of here.

92
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,788
Thank you. Our--
-[making horn noises]

93
00:04:14,855 --> 00:04:16,523
-Thank you.
Our message is a simple one.

94
00:04:16,590 --> 00:04:17,725
-[making horn noises]

95
00:04:17,792 --> 00:04:19,927
-Crow. Crow...

96
00:04:19,993 --> 00:04:22,830
For we have struggled,
yet we have prevailed...

97
00:04:22,897 --> 00:04:25,467
-[making horn noises]
-...through-- please. Thank you.

98
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:28,168
Through the dark days of Outlaw--
-[making horn noises]

99
00:04:28,235 --> 00:04:30,003
-And-- and The Creeping Terror...

100
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:33,875
[making horn noises] Hey!

101
00:04:33,942 --> 00:04:37,512
-...that we shall triumph,
for we are somebody.

102
00:04:37,578 --> 00:04:38,612
-Yeah!

103
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:40,113
-Oh, really?

104
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:42,917
Even if I tell you that
The Beast of Yucca Flats

105
00:04:42,983 --> 00:04:46,753
is another motion picture
from Coleman Francis?

106
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:49,757
-Well, I think we can survive.

107
00:04:49,823 --> 00:04:50,925
-We're doomed!

108
00:04:50,992 --> 00:04:52,693
-We have been forsaken.

109
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,328
[crying]

110
00:04:54,695 --> 00:04:56,130
-I thought so.

111
00:04:56,197 --> 00:04:58,933
So without further delay,
be prepared

112
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,635
to be crushed by
The Beast of Yucca--

113
00:05:01,702 --> 00:05:04,672
-Actually, uh,
there's a short first.

114
00:05:04,738 --> 00:05:08,642
-After the short,
be prepared to be crushed by--

115
00:05:08,710 --> 00:05:11,512
-Oh, uh, actually there's
another short after that.

116
00:05:11,578 --> 00:05:13,915
-In about a half an hour.
Would that work?

117
00:05:13,982 --> 00:05:18,953
Be prepared to be crushed
by The Beast of Yucca Flats!

118
00:05:19,020 --> 00:05:20,788
-Come on.
We can do it, guys.

119
00:05:20,855 --> 00:05:23,023
The dream will never die.

120
00:05:23,925 --> 00:05:25,360
-[crying]
-[movie sign buzzer]

121
00:05:25,427 --> 00:05:26,560
-Oh, we got Movie Sign!

122
00:05:26,627 --> 00:05:28,428
-Oh, we got Movie Sign!

123
00:05:39,807 --> 00:05:41,308
[music playing]

124
00:05:41,375 --> 00:05:42,477
-[Crow and Servo crying]

125
00:05:42,543 --> 00:05:43,677
-[Mike] Oh, come on.
It's gut check time.

126
00:05:43,745 --> 00:05:44,745
We can do it.

127
00:05:44,812 --> 00:05:47,648
-[Crow] And talks and talks.
I can't get a word in edgewise.

128
00:05:48,783 --> 00:05:51,285
-[Servo] Ah, for high school
students from 7 to 70.

129
00:05:51,352 --> 00:05:53,320
-[Mike] I'll bet high school
students flocked

130
00:05:53,387 --> 00:05:54,955
to this movie in droves.

131
00:05:58,558 --> 00:06:00,193
-Produced by imps!

132
00:06:00,595 --> 00:06:03,597
-[Servo] Promoting dullardism throughout
this great land of ours.

133
00:06:03,663 --> 00:06:04,832
[music playing]

134
00:06:04,932 --> 00:06:06,500
[Crow and Servo humming with music]

135
00:06:07,502 --> 00:06:09,937
-[Servo] Money is fun.
-[laughter]

136
00:06:10,003 --> 00:06:11,072
-[Crow] When it's fun.

137
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:15,275
-[Crow] OK, so we steal
the money tonight.

138
00:06:16,810 --> 00:06:18,813
-[Servo] Ooh, he's had his
chest excavated.

139
00:06:24,152 --> 00:06:26,753
-[Mike] Greasy scarecrow boy not
invited.

140
00:06:28,588 --> 00:06:30,658
-Want to go to the dance with me?

141
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:35,095
-[boy, voiceover] Well, here we go again.

142
00:06:35,763 --> 00:06:39,800
Why is it that I always run out of money
just when I need it?

143
00:06:39,867 --> 00:06:40,968
-[Servo] Why do I caulk my hair?

144
00:06:41,035 --> 00:06:42,537
-[boy] Why am I always broke?

145
00:06:42,603 --> 00:06:44,572
-Maybe it's my crack habit.

146
00:06:44,638 --> 00:06:48,642
-[boy] Bob buys himself a car,
while I have to worry about

147
00:06:48,708 --> 00:06:51,145
wearing a hat
to take his sister to a dance.

148
00:06:51,212 --> 00:06:52,513
-[Crow] Maybe it's these
mortgage payments.

149
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:54,682
Should have bought
a smaller house.

150
00:06:55,148 --> 00:06:56,383
-[boy] I don't get it.

151
00:06:56,450 --> 00:06:57,718
-[Servo] Ah, the appeal of Adam Sandler.

152
00:06:57,785 --> 00:07:01,188
-[boy] Other people don't seem to worry
about money all the time.

153
00:07:01,988 --> 00:07:03,892
Why am I always in the red?

154
00:07:06,093 --> 00:07:08,495
-[Crow] Even having a huge
Mallomar doesn't help.

155
00:07:08,562 --> 00:07:09,730
-[boy] $0.50.

156
00:07:10,765 --> 00:07:11,865
Half a dollar.

157
00:07:11,932 --> 00:07:13,868
-[Servo] In those days,
that'd buy you a car.

158
00:07:14,768 --> 00:07:16,137
-[boy] Benjamin Franklin, eh?

159
00:07:16,203 --> 00:07:17,205
-Bite me, Franklin.

160
00:07:17,272 --> 00:07:20,407
-[boy] He was supposed to be a pretty
smart fellow when it came to money.

161
00:07:21,542 --> 00:07:24,078
I suppose he could have told me
how to keep out of the red.

162
00:07:24,145 --> 00:07:26,213
-He was the best
president we ever had.

163
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,915
-[boy] Aw, what's the use?

164
00:07:30,117 --> 00:07:32,587
-[Servo] Sorcerer!
-[shivers]

165
00:07:32,753 --> 00:07:35,490
-[Mike] Why must I be a young
Christopher Walken?

166
00:07:36,557 --> 00:07:38,225
-There's no place like a bank.

167
00:07:38,292 --> 00:07:39,993
There's no place like a bank.

168
00:07:42,930 --> 00:07:44,232
-[Servo] Alfred Hitchcock!

169
00:07:44,298 --> 00:07:45,500
-[man] William.

170
00:07:45,567 --> 00:07:46,733
William, my boy.

171
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,435
-[Mike] Can you borrow me $1.00?

172
00:07:49,870 --> 00:07:50,938
-Who's that?

173
00:07:51,438 --> 00:07:52,540
-[man] Over here, son.

174
00:07:52,607 --> 00:07:54,508
-[Crow] Directly in front of you.

175
00:07:54,575 --> 00:07:56,477
-[Servo] Tom Bosley's come to haunt him.

176
00:07:56,943 --> 00:07:58,847
-Don't you recognize me?

177
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:01,848
You were just looking at
me on that half dollar.

178
00:08:02,250 --> 00:08:04,218
-[Mike] Just reach for the gun.

179
00:08:05,285 --> 00:08:07,322
-Are you Benjamin Franklin?

180
00:08:07,388 --> 00:08:09,523
-[Benjamin] That's right.
Come over here, son.

181
00:08:09,590 --> 00:08:10,758
I'd like to talk to you.

182
00:08:10,825 --> 00:08:12,993
-Could you have your slave press my suit?

183
00:08:14,862 --> 00:08:17,030
-[Benjamin] That's right. Over here.

184
00:08:17,298 --> 00:08:19,167
-[Servo laughs]
-Thank you, boy.

185
00:08:20,033 --> 00:08:22,203
Perhaps I can be
of some help to you

186
00:08:22,270 --> 00:08:25,773
in removing you from what you
so quaintly describe as "the red".

187
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:27,808
-[Servo] For a price!
-What do you mean?

188
00:08:27,875 --> 00:08:29,743
-Now, I don't think
that your problem

189
00:08:29,810 --> 00:08:31,612
is a difficult one, William.

190
00:08:31,678 --> 00:08:34,448
You have one important
thing to learn,

191
00:08:34,515 --> 00:08:36,550
and then you'll have no problem.

192
00:08:36,617 --> 00:08:39,220
You must learn how
to manage your money.

193
00:08:40,087 --> 00:08:41,155
-What money?

194
00:08:41,188 --> 00:08:43,357
-[Servo] Don't smart-mouth me, boy.

195
00:08:43,423 --> 00:08:44,825
-You've a point there, son.

196
00:08:44,892 --> 00:08:47,295
You must have some money
before you can manage it.

197
00:08:47,628 --> 00:08:49,863
But you do not fare
badly on that score.

198
00:08:49,930 --> 00:08:51,965
-[Servo] You can sell your body!
-I don't?

199
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:53,800
-No.

200
00:08:54,002 --> 00:08:55,102
Let me show you.

201
00:08:55,168 --> 00:08:58,638
-[Crow] Will our mystery guest
enter and sign in, please?

202
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:02,477
-[Benjamin] Come on, boy.
-[Mike] Jump on my stomach.

203
00:09:02,677 --> 00:09:04,645
-Come a little closer.

204
00:09:04,712 --> 00:09:09,717
Suppose you look in this mirror
and see what it tells you.

205
00:09:09,783 --> 00:09:10,785
-[Mike] God, I'm fat.

206
00:09:10,852 --> 00:09:15,757
-[Benjamin] Now, take a good look
at you and your earnings.

207
00:09:16,123 --> 00:09:17,458
-[Crow] I'm Kate Moss!

208
00:09:17,525 --> 00:09:21,095
-[Benjamin] You receive $2.00 every week
as an allowance from your father.

209
00:09:21,162 --> 00:09:22,162
-[Mike] James Joyce.

210
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:24,265
-[Benjamin] Something quite unheard of
in my day.

211
00:09:24,332 --> 00:09:25,465
-Fathers?

212
00:09:25,933 --> 00:09:30,237
-[Benjamin] Then, you earn about $3.00
each week delivering for the pharmacy.

213
00:09:30,303 --> 00:09:31,305
-[Servo] Here's your sherry.

214
00:09:31,372 --> 00:09:33,707
-[Benjamin] In addition,
you obtain another dollar or so

215
00:09:33,773 --> 00:09:35,242
in what you call "tips".

216
00:09:35,308 --> 00:09:36,710
-Or protection.

217
00:09:37,210 --> 00:09:39,913
-[Benjamin] You earn between $6.00
and $7.00 a week, William.

218
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:41,215
-[Mike, Servo and Crow] Ooh.

219
00:09:41,282 --> 00:09:44,285
-A tidy sum for a boy
who's still in school.

220
00:09:44,352 --> 00:09:48,255
-Maybe so, but I never have
any money when I need it.

221
00:09:48,488 --> 00:09:51,058
-That's not because you're
a poor earner, William.

222
00:09:51,225 --> 00:09:52,993
It's because you're
a poor spender.

223
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:54,262
-[Crow] And a bad person.

224
00:09:54,328 --> 00:09:55,730
-Poor spender?

225
00:09:56,163 --> 00:09:57,197
-Yes, my boy.

226
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:59,400
You spend your money
without any plan.

227
00:10:00,802 --> 00:10:02,503
You buy whenever the mood strikes you.

228
00:10:02,570 --> 00:10:04,405
-[Servo] Furs, cars, trips to Vegas.

229
00:10:04,472 --> 00:10:06,807
-[Benjamin] You spend your money as
fast as you acquire it.

230
00:10:06,873 --> 00:10:08,808
-[Servo] Ugh.
-[Benjamin] With no thought

231
00:10:08,875 --> 00:10:10,577
for the future.
-[Servo] You idiot.

232
00:10:10,645 --> 00:10:12,880
-[Benjamin] Then,
when something comes along

233
00:10:12,947 --> 00:10:15,750
where you need money,
you do not have it.

234
00:10:15,817 --> 00:10:18,385
-On behalf of all girls, none of us
are going to the dance with you.

235
00:10:18,452 --> 00:10:19,820
-I guess you're right.

236
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:21,355
But what should I do about it?

237
00:10:21,388 --> 00:10:22,390
-[Servo] I don't know!

238
00:10:22,457 --> 00:10:24,525
-Whatever you want to do, my boy.

239
00:10:24,592 --> 00:10:28,095
The important thing
is to want to do something.

240
00:10:28,528 --> 00:10:31,298
Now, judging from these drawings,

241
00:10:32,098 --> 00:10:33,900
-you'd like to be an architect someday.

242
00:10:33,967 --> 00:10:35,235
-[Servo] Forget it, soda jerk.
-That's right.

243
00:10:35,302 --> 00:10:38,305
-Fine.
Then let me ask you a question.

244
00:10:38,772 --> 00:10:41,642
Why should anyone pay an architect
for house plans?

245
00:10:41,708 --> 00:10:44,245
Why shouldn't he just go
right ahead and build it?

246
00:10:45,212 --> 00:10:46,680
