306
00:12:58,312 --> 00:13:00,747
-Huh?
-He sets that aside first.

307
00:13:00,815 --> 00:13:04,152
-[Mike] Uh.
-Boy, what willpower.

308
00:13:04,218 --> 00:13:06,153
-[Benjamin] No, it isn't just willpower.

309
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:08,855
You see, Bob had a goal.

310
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:09,923
-[Servo] And two assists!

311
00:13:09,990 --> 00:13:11,758
-He knew two years ago
that he wanted a car

312
00:13:11,825 --> 00:13:15,395
when he finished high school,
so he began saving for it.

313
00:13:16,430 --> 00:13:19,132
Each week, he went down to the bank...
-[Crow] And robbed it!

314
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:21,202
-...and deposited his savings regularly.

315
00:13:21,668 --> 00:13:23,737
And the extra money he made
during vacations

316
00:13:23,803 --> 00:13:26,207
helped his bank account grow, too.

317
00:13:26,273 --> 00:13:29,610
Until one day, he had enough
to buy the car he wanted.

318
00:13:29,677 --> 00:13:31,045
-[Mike] But then he crashed
his car and died.

319
00:13:31,112 --> 00:13:33,813
-[Benjamin] Bob remembered
one important rule.

320
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:35,182
-[Servo] Stuffing instead of potatoes.

321
00:13:35,248 --> 00:13:38,218
-[Benjamin] Save for a goal,

322
00:13:38,285 --> 00:13:40,955
so you can buy something
you really want later on.

323
00:13:41,588 --> 00:13:44,825
You see, William, it's just as true today

324
00:13:44,892 --> 00:13:47,160
as it was the first time I said it.

325
00:13:47,327 --> 00:13:50,097
"A penny saved is a penny earned."

326
00:13:50,163 --> 00:13:51,598
-Thank you. I'm out of here.

327
00:13:51,665 --> 00:13:54,968
-Now, suppose you
decided to have a budget.

328
00:13:55,035 --> 00:13:56,470
How would you start?

329
00:13:56,570 --> 00:13:58,672
-Well...
-[Mike] With lots of money.

330
00:13:58,738 --> 00:14:01,642
-The first thing I would do
is to estimate my income.

331
00:14:02,375 --> 00:14:04,578
-That's right. Figure it out.

332
00:14:04,645 --> 00:14:06,013
By the week, in your case.

333
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:07,915
-[Servo] Shouldn't take long
to estimate $0.50.

334
00:14:07,982 --> 00:14:11,985
-Estimate my income.

335
00:14:12,052 --> 00:14:13,820
-[Benjamin] Then you must decide just how

336
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:15,855
you're going to spend your money.

337
00:14:15,890 --> 00:14:16,923
-That's right.

338
00:14:16,990 --> 00:14:18,425
Plan my spending.

339
00:14:19,092 --> 00:14:22,963
Plan my spending.

340
00:14:23,030 --> 00:14:24,965
-Could you get your stomach
off my desk, please?

341
00:14:25,032 --> 00:14:26,033
-How do I do that?

342
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:27,367
-Well...

343
00:14:27,433 --> 00:14:30,037
-[Mike] Have illegitimate children.
-[robots laugh]

344
00:14:30,103 --> 00:14:33,107
