345
00:14:33,173 --> 00:14:34,742
but you'll keep
adjusting your budget

346
00:14:34,808 --> 00:14:38,378
as you go along until you get it,
so that it fits.

347
00:14:38,445 --> 00:14:40,080
And that's the third point.

348
00:14:40,147 --> 00:14:41,615
Keep it flexible.

349
00:14:42,082 --> 00:14:44,217
-Keep...
-[Mike] Pretending to write.

350
00:14:44,285 --> 00:14:46,687
-...budget flexible.

351
00:14:46,753 --> 00:14:49,957
-[Benjamin] Yes.
Do not ever let it become too rigid.

352
00:14:50,023 --> 00:14:52,292
If you do,
you'll become a prisoner to it.

353
00:14:52,358 --> 00:14:53,360
-[Mike] Hey!

354
00:14:53,427 --> 00:14:57,063
-And finally, you must
plan your savings.

355
00:14:57,130 --> 00:15:00,733
-[William] Plan my savings.

356
00:15:01,402 --> 00:15:02,770
-[Servo] William,
what are you doing in there?

357
00:15:02,837 --> 00:15:04,972
You're not talking
to the founding fathers again, are you?

358
00:15:05,038 --> 00:15:08,242
-If you'll remember these
few simple rules, William,

359
00:15:08,342 --> 00:15:13,880
